WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:08.007
[opening theme song playing]

00:45.879 --> 00:48.840
[grunting]

00:50.925 --> 00:52.010
[exhales heavily]

00:53.011 --> 00:56.765
[raindrops pattering]

01:10.320 --> 01:13.406
We're both at the drainage pumping station
and decided to get a drink.

01:13.490 --> 01:15.283
I didn't think he'd get so messy.

01:17.786 --> 01:19.370
You could've just called a taxi.

01:21.372 --> 01:23.208
It's, uh…
[chuckles]

01:24.042 --> 01:24.876
Oh?

01:26.127 --> 01:27.253
You're not staying at home?

01:30.799 --> 01:32.258
Oh, yeah.

01:33.218 --> 01:34.552
It's a long story.

01:35.386 --> 01:36.596
It's a long story.

01:38.223 --> 01:39.307
[chuckles]

01:40.099 --> 01:42.227
What were you doing?
It's weird for you to be here, too.

01:42.852 --> 01:45.271
It's a long story for me, too.

01:46.981 --> 01:48.691
Are you saying that,
'cause you don't want to answer,

01:48.775 --> 01:49.609
or 'cause you can't?

01:50.276 --> 01:51.653
I can say the same thing, director.

01:53.780 --> 01:54.614
You what?

01:54.697 --> 01:57.242
Most people would send
their drunk co-worker home in a taxi,

01:57.325 --> 01:59.661
but you took him into a motel
and tucked him in.

02:06.000 --> 02:08.336
[Ha-kyung] Past wounds are cut deep.

02:09.671 --> 02:10.505
[woman] Mr. Lee.

02:13.258 --> 02:14.926
IMI MOTEL

02:15.009 --> 02:18.054
I didn't expect you to stick around.

02:18.138 --> 02:19.639
Are you heading home?

02:21.015 --> 02:24.394
[Ha-kyung] Just when you think
the wound is healed, something happens,

02:24.477 --> 02:26.104
and you realize it's still raw.

02:26.187 --> 02:28.398
Come again, don't make this
a one-time thing.

02:29.482 --> 02:30.567
Get home safe.

02:46.374 --> 02:49.085
[Ha-kyung] The more memories you gather
where the heart is wounded,

02:49.169 --> 02:51.462
the more frightened you are
of being wounded again.

02:52.463 --> 02:55.675
Like heat that can't dissipate
trapped in a concrete jungle,

02:55.758 --> 02:59.304
you're stuck surrounded by memories,
unhealed wounds.

02:59.387 --> 03:03.057
You feel a breeze you can ride out,
and just when you think you'll get out,

03:03.141 --> 03:05.935
you feel your wound, the breeze dies down.

03:09.814 --> 03:14.694
EPISODE 6
HEAT ISLAND PHENOMENON

03:14.777 --> 03:17.697
Today, we're reporting
our first heat warning in Seoul this year.

03:17.780 --> 03:20.867
Worsened by heat islands in the city
readmitting heat from the sun,

03:20.950 --> 03:24.370
we know this scorching heat wave
is going to continue for several days.

03:24.454 --> 03:26.456
[reporter 1] Heat radiating
from asphalts in the roads,

03:26.539 --> 03:29.000
combined from the heat emitted
from the city's AC units,

03:29.083 --> 03:31.044
are likely raising temperatures
even higher.

03:31.127 --> 03:33.254
More from Reporter Park Cheol-min.

03:37.675 --> 03:39.302
[yawns]

03:42.639 --> 03:45.475
Oh, it's too early to be hot.

03:46.059 --> 03:48.144
Are you really cooking right now?
What are you making?

03:55.151 --> 03:56.110
[sighs]

03:58.238 --> 03:59.906
That time of year already?

04:01.032 --> 04:03.034
[calm music playing]

04:05.954 --> 04:07.538
Oh, Ma, it's not worth it.

04:07.622 --> 04:09.415
No one eats it, 'cause it's gross.

04:09.499 --> 04:11.334
You're spitting. Go inside.

04:11.417 --> 04:13.378
I'm worried about you staying out here.

04:15.880 --> 04:16.798
[exhales deeply]

04:17.799 --> 04:18.716
[sighs]

04:37.402 --> 04:39.279
It's monsoon season, so he…

04:39.362 --> 04:41.322
he's gonna stay at work
for a little while.

04:41.406 --> 04:43.283
Didn't he come, so he could see us?

04:43.366 --> 04:44.409
Huh?

04:45.952 --> 04:47.662
Well, yes, he did.

04:48.621 --> 04:50.290
- It was just…
- Will he come back?

04:52.583 --> 04:53.668
Uh…

04:55.044 --> 04:56.296
Sure, when the season's over.

05:08.683 --> 05:11.060
[Dong-han] Ugh, it's too hot.

05:11.144 --> 05:12.312
[groans]

05:21.070 --> 05:22.238
[sighs]

05:26.034 --> 05:27.327
Oh, shit.

05:32.582 --> 05:35.585
[groans]
It's not gonna get any hotter.

05:36.836 --> 05:38.004
Hello.

05:44.802 --> 05:46.971
[Young-gil] And the anticyclone
is staying over…

05:47.055 --> 05:48.389
Sorry I'm late.

05:48.931 --> 05:50.516
…still, everyone should stay on the…

05:57.231 --> 05:58.816
And the heat wave

05:58.900 --> 06:01.778
is bringing temperatures above average,
but only temporarily.

06:01.861 --> 06:04.447
- [Young-gil] It's warm for June.
- You sure coming early?

06:04.530 --> 06:05.406
Huh?

06:05.490 --> 06:08.242
Does the Team Two
have the night shift starting today?

06:08.868 --> 06:09.744
What today?

06:10.661 --> 06:11.662
[Sung-jin chuckles]

06:11.746 --> 06:14.373
It's a lot to keep track off.
Was it very different in Gangwon?

06:15.416 --> 06:17.085
- Goodbye.
- Nice seeing you.

06:29.305 --> 06:31.307
[light music playing]

06:47.490 --> 06:49.700
[water sloshing]

06:53.663 --> 06:55.665
[clinking]

07:01.295 --> 07:03.214
[exhales deeply]

07:04.257 --> 07:06.551
- [sniffing]
- [clanks]

07:13.224 --> 07:15.351
Butter. Butter. Butter. Butter.

07:17.770 --> 07:18.688
Butter.

07:18.771 --> 07:19.647
[groans]

07:19.730 --> 07:23.317
[breathing sharply]

07:24.360 --> 07:25.695
It smells!

07:27.155 --> 07:29.157
[playful music playing]

07:32.910 --> 07:34.912
[grunting]

07:35.788 --> 07:36.664
[sighs]

07:38.040 --> 07:42.628
INCOMING CALL
APARTMENT 1302

07:43.796 --> 07:47.967
[device ringing]

07:48.050 --> 07:50.344
CALLING
APARTMENT 1201

07:50.428 --> 07:52.430
[playful music playing]

07:53.389 --> 07:54.432
[exhales deeply]

08:21.501 --> 08:22.585
[Si-woo] Coming.

08:22.668 --> 08:23.920
[lock chimes]

08:24.003 --> 08:26.172
- Oh, you're still here.
- Oh, yeah.

08:26.255 --> 08:27.757
Uh, can I help you with something?

08:27.840 --> 08:29.842
We needed to reach you,
I have texted several times,

08:29.926 --> 08:31.969
maybe you didn't see.
Where are you gonna go?

08:32.053 --> 08:34.555
We got a word that a new trainee
is coming pretty soon,

08:34.639 --> 08:36.641
because of that,
we'd like you to move out.

08:36.724 --> 08:38.476
Ideally, by next week?

08:39.644 --> 08:40.770
Oh, so soon?

08:41.437 --> 08:45.066
There has to be enough time for repairs
and cleaning before they move in.

08:45.149 --> 08:47.652
We had expected you to find a place
after a month.

08:47.735 --> 08:49.111
You didn't know that?

08:49.195 --> 08:50.404
No, no.

08:50.488 --> 08:52.281
Let's plan on that, then. End of the week.

08:52.365 --> 08:53.991
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

09:03.709 --> 09:08.923
[cell phone buzzing]

09:16.764 --> 09:18.391
[jazz music playing]

09:27.567 --> 09:29.277
Ah, you didn't run
in this weather, did you?

09:30.069 --> 09:32.780
You don't sleep in
even when you're a night shift?

09:35.449 --> 09:36.659
Should I get something to eat?

09:38.619 --> 09:40.079
We should reconsider what we're doing.

09:41.622 --> 09:42.873
Consider what now?

09:43.624 --> 09:44.625
You and me.

09:48.045 --> 09:49.880
[Si-woo] "When one cloud meets another,

09:49.964 --> 09:52.508
there's a great noise, thunder.

09:52.592 --> 09:55.094
Like them, I want to meet you,

09:55.595 --> 09:58.764
shouting about it from the rooftops
without a thought.

10:00.641 --> 10:02.727
When one cloud
suddenly meets another cloud,

10:03.269 --> 10:05.730
there's a great light, too, lightning.

10:05.813 --> 10:07.565
With that light when I meet you,

10:07.648 --> 10:10.234
I'll see the path
I strayed from long ago."

10:12.194 --> 10:14.071
Hang on, I don't get the last part.

10:14.989 --> 10:16.115
This stanza.

10:16.198 --> 10:17.658
[Ha-kyung] "You shine like lightning

10:17.742 --> 10:20.244
as you say that a rain cloud
needs to meet another rain cloud

10:20.328 --> 10:21.412
for them to get drenched."

10:21.495 --> 10:22.330
That part.

10:22.872 --> 10:23.831
Hm…

10:25.708 --> 10:30.004
You have to find someone that's like you,
for either of you to open up and rain.

10:31.380 --> 10:32.798
Ah, that's my best guess.

10:33.674 --> 10:34.634
For example?

10:38.429 --> 10:39.555
- [chuckles]
- Let it rain.

10:39.639 --> 10:41.349
- [chuckling]
- What was that?

10:41.849 --> 10:44.185
- You're cloud?
- [Si-woo] The pain we've been though,

10:45.478 --> 10:47.271
that's what the poem was describing.

10:49.148 --> 10:52.860
"A rain cloud needs to meet another
for them to get drenched."

10:55.988 --> 10:57.323
What? Why now?

11:01.744 --> 11:04.705
Well, I thought I'd recovered.
I was wrong. I'm not.

11:08.668 --> 11:12.922
All last night, I couldn't stop thinking
about the motel when I saw you.

11:14.090 --> 11:16.342
I keep thinking
of ignoring red flags again.

11:16.926 --> 11:18.094
It's exhausting.

11:20.096 --> 11:22.264
Nothing happened with that woman,
I promise you.

11:22.348 --> 11:26.727
Yeah, and I really wanna believe you.
It'd be better for me.

11:27.353 --> 11:30.606
But I get this feeling in my stomach
every time I think about it.

11:33.984 --> 11:36.779
I know you're not the kind of person
who would lie.

11:36.862 --> 11:39.156
And then that's a problem, too.

11:39.824 --> 11:41.992
You've been nothing but honest, and I…

11:42.701 --> 11:44.495
And that's not enough, for some reason.

11:47.331 --> 11:48.290
Director Jin.

11:48.374 --> 11:50.167
We should take some time
to think about it.

11:51.919 --> 11:55.297
It's not anything you did.
I'll figure things out myself.

12:01.762 --> 12:03.347
I'm gonna head out. Enjoy.

12:06.934 --> 12:08.060
It was my dad.

12:11.522 --> 12:12.857
I only went to the motel…

12:15.818 --> 12:17.027
because I was looking for him.

12:25.828 --> 12:26.704
[woman] Mr. Lee?

12:27.496 --> 12:29.331
Lee Myung-han here. I'm his son.

12:34.336 --> 12:35.504
Go ahead.

12:37.673 --> 12:39.967
[gambler 1] Hey, why don't you just fold?

12:40.593 --> 12:42.470
[gambler 2] It's like looking at a statue.

12:43.095 --> 12:43.929
Come on.

12:44.805 --> 12:46.515
- Shit!
- Hey, pal.

12:46.599 --> 12:47.933
- [laughing]
- Your boy is here.

12:48.642 --> 12:50.978
- [indistinct chatter]
- He's very handsome.

12:51.061 --> 12:53.647
Oh, Si-woo. You're here.

12:54.940 --> 12:56.192
Hey.

12:56.275 --> 12:57.401
Hey, Si-woo!

12:57.902 --> 12:59.278
Hey, S-woo. Si…

12:59.361 --> 13:01.822
Damn it. Oh! Get back here, Si-woo!

13:01.906 --> 13:03.365
[Myung-han] Hey! Hey!

13:03.449 --> 13:05.284
Wait! Wait! Come on!

13:05.367 --> 13:07.286
Si-woo, come on.

13:08.454 --> 13:10.039
Don't walk away from me.

13:10.122 --> 13:11.957
You came all the way here
just to turn around?

13:12.041 --> 13:13.167
You're gambling again?

13:13.250 --> 13:15.753
So this is why you're blowing up my phone,
calling me non-stop?

13:16.712 --> 13:19.548
I had to. You're my only son. Come on.

13:19.632 --> 13:21.967
So, give me all the money
that you brought.

13:24.970 --> 13:26.013
What?

13:26.096 --> 13:27.306
Oh, jeez.

13:27.389 --> 13:29.183
- You forgot to bring any?
- [sighs]

13:30.392 --> 13:32.728
- Don't have any.
- I know what you do.

13:32.811 --> 13:35.147
Don't lie to me.
I know you landed a big promotion.

13:35.231 --> 13:37.191
You're rolling in cash. I know.

13:37.274 --> 13:41.320
You already burned through
everything I saved from last year.

13:42.321 --> 13:43.155
Did I really?

13:44.156 --> 13:46.742
Well, you know, I'm okay with coins, okay?
Anything works.

13:47.493 --> 13:49.495
Oh, come on. They're gonna
make me dig my own grave.

13:49.578 --> 13:51.247
I'm dying right now, so…

13:51.330 --> 13:53.290
- Just…
- Hey, I don't have any money!

13:53.374 --> 13:56.627
I had to over stay at the training center,
because I can't afford a deposit!

13:56.710 --> 13:58.128
Then get a loan.

13:58.212 --> 13:59.838
If you work for the government,

13:59.922 --> 14:02.341
you're supposed to get lots
of extra stuff.

14:03.968 --> 14:05.594
Don't ever call. I'm done with you.

14:05.678 --> 14:07.263
Contact me and I'll call the police.

14:07.346 --> 14:10.266
I'll never think about you again.
You're not my father any longer.

14:10.349 --> 14:11.892
You little…

14:11.976 --> 14:14.103
Hey, don't go. Stop.

14:14.186 --> 14:15.896
Ungrateful… Huh?

14:16.981 --> 14:18.107
[groans]
Shit.

14:19.066 --> 14:20.109
Jeez.

14:20.192 --> 14:22.194
[raindrops pattering]

14:23.612 --> 14:24.822
[Ha-kyung] What were you doing?

14:25.573 --> 14:27.199
It's weird for you to be here, too.

14:28.450 --> 14:31.161
It's a long story for me, too.

14:32.746 --> 14:34.790
Are you saying that,
'cause you don't want to answer,

14:34.874 --> 14:35.833
or 'cause you can't?

14:36.584 --> 14:38.168
I can say the same thing, director.

14:40.337 --> 14:41.589
She's a director.

14:43.841 --> 14:44.925
You what?

14:45.634 --> 14:47.970
Most people would send
their drunk co-worker home in a taxi,

14:48.637 --> 14:50.556
but you took him into a motel
and tucked him in.

15:03.986 --> 15:05.404
[lock chimes]

15:09.658 --> 15:10.868
[lock chimes]

15:14.538 --> 15:15.497
[sighs]

15:28.469 --> 15:30.471
[somber music playing]

16:05.214 --> 16:06.757
[sighs]

16:29.947 --> 16:31.115
The record's office?

16:32.116 --> 16:33.784
- Why?
- Hm?

16:34.576 --> 16:35.619
For our marriage license.

16:36.453 --> 16:38.622
It's filled out,
we just have to turn it in,

16:38.706 --> 16:41.458
then we're eligible for a housing loan
as a married couple.

16:42.376 --> 16:43.544
Uh-huh.

16:44.420 --> 16:46.839
And you don't want to renew our lease
for the apartment?

16:46.922 --> 16:49.216
It's out of the budget and no amenities.

16:50.050 --> 16:50.968
Mm.

16:56.015 --> 16:57.641
Okay, what's wrong?

16:59.893 --> 17:01.061
You didn't…

17:03.439 --> 17:05.190
get attached to that apartment already.

17:06.608 --> 17:07.568
Guess I did.

17:08.235 --> 17:09.820
Oh…

17:11.363 --> 17:12.322
Yu-jin.

17:13.574 --> 17:16.368
Our home is anywhere we can be together.

17:16.452 --> 17:17.995
That's what matters. It'll grow on you.

17:18.871 --> 17:21.331
I'll find us somewhere really nice,
I promise you.

17:21.415 --> 17:22.458
[chuckles]

17:23.876 --> 17:26.962
Right. I'll send you with my seal
and ID card,

17:27.046 --> 17:29.256
and you can turn everything in
for both of us?

17:29.339 --> 17:30.758
I wish I could go, too.

17:30.841 --> 17:32.801
But I've gotta get
my column done for tomorrow.

17:32.885 --> 17:35.054
- Is that okay?
- Sure.

17:35.137 --> 17:36.138
That's great.

17:41.351 --> 17:42.895
- Want mine as well?
- Hm?

17:44.146 --> 17:45.606
You barely touched it.

17:45.689 --> 17:46.982
Don't you like chicken?

17:50.027 --> 17:52.696
Wow, the drumstick.
[chuckles]

17:54.406 --> 17:55.491
Mmm.

17:57.618 --> 17:58.786
[both chuckle]

18:03.499 --> 18:05.375
- Have you eaten?
- Yes, sir.

18:06.627 --> 18:08.087
- Did you have lunch?
- Oh, yeah.

18:09.046 --> 18:11.673
There's a lot to do today,
so gimbap works for me.

18:11.757 --> 18:17.221
Hey, now. Gimbap is basically a snack.
Eating enough is more important than work.

18:17.304 --> 18:18.138
Yup.

18:18.722 --> 18:21.225
- So, uh, what are you working so hard?
- It…

18:21.308 --> 18:22.226
It's nothing.

18:22.309 --> 18:23.602
No, come on.

18:24.561 --> 18:27.773
Well, the director asked me
for a column for internal use.

18:28.357 --> 18:30.025
A column? What about?

18:31.276 --> 18:33.195
- About the month.
- About…

18:34.905 --> 18:37.282
What do you mean?
You're writing monthly column?

18:38.742 --> 18:39.910
I asked him to give it a try.

18:40.869 --> 18:42.788
But that's… It's just I write that column.

18:42.871 --> 18:45.541
Well, it's not ready
and we have to send it to print soon.

18:45.624 --> 18:47.626
You're late and there's a deadline.

18:47.709 --> 18:49.920
I needed a backup.
I can't just hope you'll get it done.

18:50.504 --> 18:53.048
I just wanted to proofread it
a little more.

18:53.632 --> 18:55.634
It's basically completely ready to print.

18:55.717 --> 18:57.427
Right then, wrap it up and let me see.

18:58.262 --> 18:59.388
And Min-jun?

18:59.471 --> 19:01.473
Min-jun, I still wanna see yours, too.

19:02.099 --> 19:03.600
I want both columns.

19:03.684 --> 19:06.478
We'll print whichever's better.
I'll decide. All right?

19:09.273 --> 19:11.150
Assistant Director Kim, good luck.

19:12.651 --> 19:14.153
[inhales deeply]
You as well.

19:14.820 --> 19:16.905
- Yeah.
- [Ju-won] Good luck to both of you. Hm?

19:18.615 --> 19:20.784
Mr. Han, good luck.

19:20.868 --> 19:23.203
Thanks. You too.

19:29.084 --> 19:30.377
It's fine.

19:30.460 --> 19:31.837
[objects clattering]

19:31.920 --> 19:35.591
I'll get it done. He'll see.
I'll get it done.

19:36.258 --> 19:39.011
He'll see. All right, let's go.

19:40.971 --> 19:42.139
[clears throat]

19:43.265 --> 19:46.018
[keyboard clacking]

19:46.101 --> 19:49.188
MARRIAGE CERTIFICATE

19:49.271 --> 19:52.191
WIFE
SEAL OR SIGNATURE

20:00.866 --> 20:02.868
[somber music playing]

20:15.714 --> 20:17.799
- I'm going home. Goodbye.
- Mm.

20:18.884 --> 20:20.886
[keyboard clacking]

20:23.347 --> 20:24.181
[clicks]

20:25.140 --> 20:26.058
That's it.

20:27.643 --> 20:29.186
- You're done?
- Yeah.

20:29.937 --> 20:31.271
Oh, you're not?

20:31.980 --> 20:33.023
Uh…

20:33.523 --> 20:37.027
I still have lots and lots
of, um, other report to get through.

20:37.611 --> 20:39.279
It goes on and on.

20:39.363 --> 20:40.197
[chuckles]

20:40.739 --> 20:42.241
Don't worry about me, though. Go home.

20:42.324 --> 20:44.201
- Okay.
- [mouse clicking]

20:47.329 --> 20:49.539
I'll see you. Tomorrow, then.

20:49.623 --> 20:50.457
Yeah.

20:51.625 --> 20:52.834
Good night.

20:58.632 --> 20:59.841
[door closes]

21:01.385 --> 21:02.594
[groans]

21:04.680 --> 21:07.266
[whines]

21:14.231 --> 21:15.732
Oh, you're here early.

21:15.816 --> 21:18.360
I forgot the schedule flipped
and we were night shift.

21:18.443 --> 21:19.778
I was 12 hours early.

21:20.320 --> 21:23.532
Oh, I thought I was late this morning,
so I rushed over here.

21:23.615 --> 21:25.284
And I ran to Team One.

21:25.367 --> 21:27.661
Maybe you should try
to be early to our team meetings,

21:27.744 --> 21:29.746
and go late to theirs instead, okay?

21:29.830 --> 21:30.831
[both chuckle]

21:31.498 --> 21:34.626
And, hey, you could've just
left me last night when I got drunk.

21:34.710 --> 21:36.169
I'm sure I was a lot.

21:36.253 --> 21:38.797
We're well into monsoon season.
It's hectic.

21:38.880 --> 21:41.133
I couldn't have you out for a day.
We're all hands on deck.

21:41.216 --> 21:43.844
I need you here.
A valued and crucial team member.

21:43.927 --> 21:46.138
[sighs]
Crucial. I'm more of a burden.

21:47.097 --> 21:49.766
- Did you have dinner?
- Not yet. I'm not that hungry.

21:49.850 --> 21:52.436
I'll see you in 30.
Go get something to eat.

21:53.437 --> 21:54.604
Well…

21:55.439 --> 21:58.275
- [doors slide]
- [chuckles]

21:59.609 --> 22:00.694
Whoa.

22:01.737 --> 22:02.696
What is it?

22:06.199 --> 22:07.326
What?

22:09.286 --> 22:11.288
[quirky music playing]

22:14.666 --> 22:16.376
Why was he glaring at me?

22:19.296 --> 22:20.422
- Hello.
- Hello.

22:29.765 --> 22:31.141
Hey, I had dinner.

22:36.563 --> 22:39.441
[Dong-han] What did I miss? Hm?

22:40.942 --> 22:42.861
[Young-gil] The temperature is fairly high

22:42.944 --> 22:44.571
and the radiation is keeping up.

22:44.654 --> 22:45.614
The sun is about to set,

22:45.697 --> 22:48.158
but the temperature is
still 28 degree Celcius.

22:48.658 --> 22:51.369
I think this heat island
could really melt Seoul to the ground.

22:52.162 --> 22:54.414
Do you think the atmospheric flow
will stay constant?

22:54.498 --> 22:55.582
Who's to say?

22:55.665 --> 22:58.668
We can always get rain out of nowhere.
That seems to happen a lot.

22:58.752 --> 22:59.586
[chuckles]

23:09.721 --> 23:11.056
[cell phone buzzes]

23:13.850 --> 23:16.103
[Tae-kyung] Call me now.
Something's wrong with Mom.

23:21.066 --> 23:22.109
Careful.

23:26.613 --> 23:27.656
Oh…

23:31.493 --> 23:32.452
[sighs]

23:37.290 --> 23:38.250
[scoffs]

23:38.333 --> 23:41.044
You're telling me she can't call?
I told her you're under the weather.

23:41.128 --> 23:42.671
It's fine.

23:43.588 --> 23:46.007
I think she's on night shift
starting today.

23:46.091 --> 23:49.344
She could text at least. It's selfish.
And she should be worried about you.

23:49.427 --> 23:51.304
You treat her like a child, and she's not.

23:51.388 --> 23:53.431
She's an adult and selfish.
[clicks tongue]

23:53.932 --> 23:56.309
I bet she thinks it's another trick.

23:57.060 --> 24:00.230
"Oh, our mom is sick
and you need to come over right away."

24:01.314 --> 24:02.149
[cell phone chimes]

24:03.191 --> 24:04.818
[line rings]

24:04.901 --> 24:05.819
TAE-KYUNG

24:07.571 --> 24:09.781
Do you have anything
on probability of rain tonight?

24:11.283 --> 24:14.161
Wow. Who does she think she is?

24:15.829 --> 24:16.746
[Tae-kyung scoffs]

24:18.832 --> 24:21.835
SUPPLEMENTARY WEATHER CHART

24:32.512 --> 24:35.098
It's really so quiet.

24:35.182 --> 24:36.433
It can't always be chaos.

24:37.267 --> 24:39.603
There's still a chance
of localized heavy rain.

24:39.686 --> 24:41.313
Stay alert, everyone.

24:41.396 --> 24:42.606
- Okay.
- Sure.

24:55.911 --> 24:56.870
[sighs]

25:11.343 --> 25:13.220
Hey, are you okay?

25:16.139 --> 25:16.973
Huh?

25:17.557 --> 25:18.808
Are you saying something?

25:19.726 --> 25:22.020
It seems like something
is distracting you today.

25:22.103 --> 25:23.021
Oh.

25:23.772 --> 25:26.733
Well, it's just… family stuff.

25:26.816 --> 25:29.152
[Myung-ju chuckles]

25:35.033 --> 25:35.867
Honey.

25:37.494 --> 25:41.456
I wanna take the Level Five
technical exam again.

25:43.541 --> 25:44.709
[sighs]

25:55.679 --> 25:57.097
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

25:57.180 --> 25:58.598
[phone ringing]

26:02.435 --> 26:04.062
- Director Jin.
- Huh?

26:04.145 --> 26:05.563
Should I answer the phone for you?

26:05.647 --> 26:06.773
Oh, no, it's all right.

26:08.024 --> 26:10.151
Director Jin of Team Two speaking.

26:13.238 --> 26:14.281
What?

26:14.364 --> 26:16.908
He's here, ma'am. He says he knows you.

26:17.701 --> 26:19.744
He says it's urgent
and he wants to see you.

26:19.828 --> 26:20.954
What should I tell him?

26:21.538 --> 26:22.706
Ah, of course.

26:22.789 --> 26:23.748
Let me.

26:25.417 --> 26:26.835
Hi. Hello, director.

26:27.335 --> 26:29.713
I'm Lee Myung-han.

26:29.796 --> 26:31.715
Lee Si-woo's my son, you know.

26:37.637 --> 26:40.682
The thing is,
there's lots we gotta discuss.

26:40.765 --> 26:42.517
The stuff you should know
regarding Si-woo.

26:42.600 --> 26:43.518
So can you…

26:44.519 --> 26:47.272
can you spare just ten minutes
of your time to chat?

26:48.523 --> 26:49.649
Okay.

27:09.377 --> 27:10.712
[sighs]

27:10.795 --> 27:13.715
What an ungrateful brat.
Why hasn't she called?

27:24.893 --> 27:26.895
[playful music playing]

27:38.865 --> 27:40.116
Oh, damn it.

27:55.423 --> 27:57.425
It's fine. No, no, no, no…

27:58.760 --> 28:00.261
[exhales heavily]

28:11.356 --> 28:13.858
[mumbling]
Don't… What am I gonna do?

28:14.484 --> 28:15.819
[muttering]

28:15.902 --> 28:18.029
[breathes deeply]

28:28.289 --> 28:29.874
You are Lee Si-woo's father?

28:30.959 --> 28:32.127
Yeah, that's right.

28:32.961 --> 28:34.003
Si-woo's my son.

28:34.712 --> 28:36.464
I see. Hello.

28:38.383 --> 28:40.385
So, what can I do for you?

28:45.515 --> 28:48.560
Actually, I gotta ask you
something important.

28:52.147 --> 28:53.064
[chuckles]

28:53.148 --> 28:55.984
Oh, jeez. I don't… I don't know
how to say this to a stranger.

28:57.444 --> 29:01.364
Then again, we're not strangers
it you have something with my son.

29:04.075 --> 29:05.368
What are you referring to?

29:05.452 --> 29:08.329
I'm referring to seeing you and my son…

29:09.247 --> 29:11.958
being close enough
to hit the motel together.

29:17.046 --> 29:17.922
Ah.

29:18.006 --> 29:20.091
I see. You haven't told anyone.

29:21.551 --> 29:23.720
[chuckles]
Okay, okay. I get it.

29:23.803 --> 29:25.138
I won't talk too loud.

29:25.221 --> 29:27.223
[chuckles nervously]

29:27.932 --> 29:32.854
Anyway, it's true that… that you two
are a couple, aren't you?

29:32.937 --> 29:33.855
Huh?

29:37.776 --> 29:40.111
I know what I saw
at that motel last night.

29:46.826 --> 29:48.244
[chuckles nervously]

29:49.287 --> 29:51.581
Sorry, what did you need
to discuss so urgently?

29:51.664 --> 29:52.874
How much cash you got?

29:54.834 --> 29:59.297
Seems to me you outranked my boy,
you're older than him, too, for sure.

29:59.881 --> 30:01.424
And your title sounds real important.

30:01.508 --> 30:05.887
So I'd guess your salary
beats Si-woo's flat out, right?

30:06.471 --> 30:09.057
See, I really need money.

30:09.140 --> 30:10.975
And I needed it yesterday, right?

30:11.059 --> 30:12.894
Would you find it in your heart
to lend me any?

30:24.697 --> 30:27.659
[doors slide close]

30:33.373 --> 30:34.499
Hey.

30:34.582 --> 30:36.251
Do you know where Director Jin went?

30:36.793 --> 30:39.420
- I think she got a call and walk out.
- I don't know.

30:41.840 --> 30:43.883
- Try calling her if you have to.
- Okay.

30:51.850 --> 30:55.728
[cell phone buzzing]

30:56.604 --> 30:58.940
TAE-KYUNG

31:06.406 --> 31:08.825
This is the phone
of Director Jin Ha-kyung.

31:10.869 --> 31:11.703
What?

31:11.786 --> 31:13.788
[tense music playing]

31:31.180 --> 31:33.725
- All right, ma'am. Please climb in.
- [whimpers]

31:35.143 --> 31:37.312
911 EMERGENCY
AMBULANCE

31:37.395 --> 31:40.899
[siren wailing]

31:42.525 --> 31:44.777
Sir, shouldn't we tell
the director to go home?

31:45.695 --> 31:48.406
She'd never listen to
the assistant director saying she should.

31:52.452 --> 31:53.995
What do you think, Mr. Um?

32:01.878 --> 32:03.880
[tense music playing]

32:21.648 --> 32:22.774
Director Jin.

32:25.360 --> 32:27.278
I picked up your phone,
'cause your sister called.

32:28.363 --> 32:29.739
She said your mom is really sick.

32:30.323 --> 32:31.407
Here.

32:36.329 --> 32:37.413
You should call them.

32:38.498 --> 32:39.499
Oh.

32:39.999 --> 32:41.542
It's not. She's done this before.

32:41.626 --> 32:43.419
My mom only gets sick
when we've been fighting.

32:43.503 --> 32:44.712
I'm sure she's just fine.

32:45.463 --> 32:47.632
- Let's go.
- They're taking her to the ER.

32:48.549 --> 32:49.509
Seriously?

32:49.592 --> 32:52.345
Your sister called an ambulance,
and she was crying really hard.

32:53.304 --> 32:55.515
I don't think
they're just trying to trick you.

32:55.598 --> 32:57.600
[ominous music playing]

32:58.851 --> 33:01.104
Jin Ha-kyung. Why aren't you here?

33:01.604 --> 33:03.398
I told you Mom's not well.

33:03.481 --> 33:05.775
I know you're mad
about the matchmaker thing.

33:05.858 --> 33:07.360
Do you care about Mom at all?

33:07.443 --> 33:10.571
I thought even you would at least call
and ask how she's doing.

33:11.322 --> 33:12.532
[sobs]

33:12.615 --> 33:14.617
[sirens wailing]

33:16.911 --> 33:20.832
Our mom is dying.
We're gonna be all alone.

33:22.750 --> 33:24.585
[crying]

33:24.669 --> 33:27.463
- What hospital are they taking her to?
- [Tae-kyung] I don't know.

33:27.547 --> 33:30.133
They just said we're going to
whichever one can be in fastest.

33:30.216 --> 33:31.050
I'll call.

33:31.134 --> 33:33.636
Okay, then. I'm on night shift,
so I'll come when I can.

33:33.720 --> 33:35.847
Did you hear me? Mom is dying!

33:36.723 --> 33:38.933
They need me.
I can't leave until my shift's done.

33:39.017 --> 33:40.935
I don't care! We need you, too!

33:41.019 --> 33:44.272
I can't leave yet.
As soon as the morning team comes.

33:44.355 --> 33:47.066
I can't believe you! Whatever!
I'm hanging up!

33:51.779 --> 33:52.613
Ma'am.

33:54.866 --> 33:56.534
I'm all right. Get back to work.

33:59.245 --> 34:00.288
[Dong-han] Director Jin.

34:02.540 --> 34:03.750
Ah…

34:05.334 --> 34:08.379
I just checked,
since anticyclone's maintaining position,

34:08.463 --> 34:10.757
there won't be atmosphere changes
till tomorrow.

34:10.840 --> 34:12.592
It's gonna probably stay hot
from the heat island.

34:12.675 --> 34:14.052
It'll be hot again during the day.

34:14.135 --> 34:18.014
Anyway, seems like it'll be constant
and steady weather till next shift.

34:18.598 --> 34:19.724
I believe you should go.

34:22.477 --> 34:24.145
I promise I'll handle things
till you're back.

34:31.027 --> 34:31.986
You don't trust me?

34:33.571 --> 34:37.033
You trust that we'll do our best
on the work that you assign us, don't you?

34:38.659 --> 34:40.078
You know that I trust you.

34:40.578 --> 34:43.247
It's my job, though.
It's my job to oversee the team.

34:43.331 --> 34:45.500
- It's not about--
- Everyone here knows what you must do.

34:45.583 --> 34:47.251
How much you care about everything.

34:47.335 --> 34:50.505
But your responsibility now
is to be a good daughter, so go.

34:54.926 --> 34:56.844
I owe you one. Please, go now.

35:03.267 --> 35:04.393
We'll be fine.

35:07.563 --> 35:09.732
Tell me you'll call
if something happens, okay?

35:16.781 --> 35:18.032
[Dong-han] Mr. Lee.

35:18.783 --> 35:19.951
Come on.

35:20.034 --> 35:21.619
Yeah. Coming, sir.

35:42.431 --> 35:44.016
What happened? How is she?

35:44.100 --> 35:46.102
[panting]

35:46.894 --> 35:48.020
[Tae-kyung] I don't know.

35:48.104 --> 35:49.981
They took blood
and did an X-ray, that's all.

35:51.190 --> 35:53.568
She said she felt weak
and had to lie down.

35:53.651 --> 35:55.153
She kept saying she was dizzy.

35:56.320 --> 35:57.989
She kept throwing up if she tried to eat.

35:58.072 --> 36:00.366
And then she got up to go to the bathroom,

36:01.868 --> 36:05.079
she lost her balance
and hit her head when she went down.

36:05.163 --> 36:06.831
[sobbing]

36:07.665 --> 36:11.460
And her… her forehead
was bleeding so much blood.

36:12.670 --> 36:16.632
I really thought that she could've died
right there and you weren't here!

36:22.889 --> 36:24.056
What were the test results?

36:25.933 --> 36:27.602
There aren't any yet.

36:27.685 --> 36:32.023
There are so many other patients today
that everything's taking longer.

36:43.576 --> 36:45.578
[calm music playing]

36:51.667 --> 36:52.627
Mr. Um.

36:52.710 --> 36:54.712
- Here's the data you wanted.
- Wow.

36:55.379 --> 36:57.548
All right, could you check
Seoul's ground-surface temperature

36:57.632 --> 36:59.884
and radiation
every ten minutes or so, please?

36:59.967 --> 37:01.052
Yes, of course.

37:02.220 --> 37:04.305
You're keeping an eye
on the anticyclone's path, right?

37:04.388 --> 37:08.059
Yeah. I really don't think
it'll change anytime soon.

37:08.142 --> 37:10.269
Hm, then let me know
if it speeds up at all.

37:10.353 --> 37:11.437
Yes, sir.

37:11.520 --> 37:12.605
[clears throat]

37:13.940 --> 37:15.942
["Something Precious" by Rothy playing]

37:26.369 --> 37:29.622
SAFE COUNTRY, PEACEFUL PEOPLE

37:39.674 --> 37:40.883
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

37:46.931 --> 37:48.307
[cell phone buzzes]

37:51.269 --> 37:53.020
[Si-woo] Did you make it
to the hospital okay?

38:16.043 --> 38:17.420
[sighs]

38:17.503 --> 38:18.587
What am I gonna do?

38:19.380 --> 38:20.506
[blows air]

38:29.140 --> 38:29.974
Jin…

38:31.142 --> 38:32.685
JIN HA-KYUNG

38:38.399 --> 38:40.109
I can't.

38:40.860 --> 38:41.819
[sighs]

38:45.072 --> 38:46.282
[grumbles]

38:50.745 --> 38:52.038
[mutters]

39:01.756 --> 39:04.925
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

39:05.634 --> 39:06.886
Good morning.

39:06.969 --> 39:09.138
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

39:09.764 --> 39:13.517
[overlapping chatter]

39:31.952 --> 39:33.496
Where is she?

39:33.579 --> 39:35.790
Did she call out? Is she gonna be late?

39:38.084 --> 39:39.794
Oh, no. No.

39:44.131 --> 39:45.925
I thought it went well.

39:46.008 --> 39:47.218
Han? What brings you here?

39:47.301 --> 39:48.469
[Myung-ju] Goodness.

39:48.552 --> 39:50.805
- Have you been here all night?
- [chuckles]

39:50.888 --> 39:52.348
I was. There was so much work to do.

39:52.431 --> 39:53.265
[Ki-jun] Yeah.

39:53.349 --> 39:56.477
Oh, and, uh, I didn't see
Director Jin come out.

39:56.560 --> 39:57.770
Where is she?

39:57.853 --> 39:59.730
Well, she had to leave for her reasons.

39:59.814 --> 40:01.273
Oh, reasons.

40:01.357 --> 40:04.318
Why do you need the director
so early after the shift's over?

40:05.111 --> 40:07.863
It's not particularly important.
Don't worry about it.

40:09.156 --> 40:11.200
- I'm getting hangover soup. Any takers?
- Ooh.

40:11.283 --> 40:12.451
- Hey.
- I'll go.

40:12.535 --> 40:13.411
- Sounds good.
- Yes.

40:13.494 --> 40:15.246
- Let's go.
- Enjoy your food, everyone.

40:15.329 --> 40:16.705
- [Dong-han] Thanks.
- [Ki-jun] Bye.

40:21.252 --> 40:22.294
[sighs]

40:23.087 --> 40:25.131
How am I supposed
to get this done in time?

40:26.298 --> 40:28.926
Why does he come to our department
so much all of a sudden?

40:29.009 --> 40:32.263
Yeah, it's weird. He's so smug.
Like we all don't know he's a cheater.

40:32.346 --> 40:33.180
It's gross.

40:33.264 --> 40:34.974
I feel like he's always there.

40:35.057 --> 40:37.226
It's 'cause he's desperate
and doesn't know what to do.

40:37.309 --> 40:38.394
Why is he desperate?

40:38.477 --> 40:40.312
- The column.
- [Soo-jin] His column?

40:40.396 --> 40:41.272
You mean,

40:42.064 --> 40:43.607
- the monthly story column?
- Mm.

40:43.691 --> 40:46.360
Director Jin ghost wrote
every single one, but he gets credit.

40:46.444 --> 40:48.487
Huh? But he gets credit?

40:48.571 --> 40:50.030
I'm sure lots of people know.

40:50.656 --> 40:52.199
You knew, right, Mr. Shin?

40:53.200 --> 40:54.535
[Myung-ju] See? Even he knew.

40:54.618 --> 40:57.872
Gosh. What a jerk. I hope he gets caught.

40:57.955 --> 41:02.168
Honestly, I think Director Jin
is a little softer than she could be.

41:02.710 --> 41:03.627
Mr. Shin?

41:07.131 --> 41:08.257
[female voice] Doors opening.

41:11.093 --> 41:12.595
Uh, actually, I've gotta get home.

41:12.678 --> 41:14.263
Why? You're not in the mood for soup?

41:14.346 --> 41:16.640
No, I had a big lunch.
I'll see you next shift.

41:16.724 --> 41:17.600
- Okay.
- Bye.

41:17.683 --> 41:18.559
- Goodbye.
- Bye.

41:19.560 --> 41:21.520
Can we get some fish tonight
instead of the beef?

41:21.604 --> 41:23.439
- Sure. Sounds good.
- [Soo-jin] Sounds delicious.

41:23.522 --> 41:26.025
[director 1] I clearly asked
for all the meteorological day scripts.

41:26.108 --> 41:27.776
What part of that didn't get through?

41:27.860 --> 41:29.695
Who told you to summarize them?

41:29.778 --> 41:32.114
Well, since the details of
the Administrator's speech weren't…

41:32.198 --> 41:34.533
relevant for the part of planning,
I thought I'd save you time.

41:34.617 --> 41:36.327
No one told you to make that call.

41:36.410 --> 41:38.078
I'm the director.

41:38.913 --> 41:39.747
Uh, sorry, sir.

41:39.830 --> 41:42.458
[director 1] I'm getting tired
of these mistakes.

41:43.709 --> 41:45.127
Fix it by tomorrow.

41:50.424 --> 41:51.425
[exhales deeply]

42:00.518 --> 42:01.644
Mr. Shin.

42:19.119 --> 42:20.204
Here.

42:21.539 --> 42:22.373
Did you eat?

42:22.456 --> 42:25.709
Of course, I had breakfast with the kids.
The soup you made was good.

42:25.793 --> 42:27.336
Huh, the kids made it to school?

42:27.419 --> 42:28.671
Yeah. Of course.

42:32.299 --> 42:34.552
You know our son wants
to start art classes.

42:35.886 --> 42:39.014
English, math, taekwondo,
and art to top it off?

42:39.098 --> 42:40.224
[chuckles]

42:41.392 --> 42:44.019
It's gonna be 800,000,
900,000 won a month.

42:46.063 --> 42:47.898
And do the same thing for our other son.

42:49.024 --> 42:50.693
Yeah. I know.

42:57.825 --> 42:59.201
You think just one year is enough?

43:01.120 --> 43:03.622
'Cause I can't do longer than that
by myself.

43:04.665 --> 43:05.833
Myung-ju.

43:07.626 --> 43:09.795
If you can promise me
you'll be working again in a year,

43:09.878 --> 43:11.964
even if you don't pass the exam,

43:12.631 --> 43:16.010
if you'll promise,
then I can hold on for a year.

43:16.093 --> 43:18.220
[breathes deeply]

43:20.639 --> 43:21.932
Oh…
[sniffles]

43:25.019 --> 43:28.314
How'd you get so lucky
to get me for a wife?

43:28.397 --> 43:30.816
[both laughing]

43:30.899 --> 43:32.109
I wish I knew.

43:32.901 --> 43:34.445
I'm the luckiest.

43:34.528 --> 43:37.323
[laughing]

43:38.741 --> 43:40.618
I promise, honey.

43:41.619 --> 43:43.495
And I promise I'll pass the test.

43:43.579 --> 43:45.497
[sobbing]

43:51.503 --> 43:53.297
Just look at you, my husband.

43:53.922 --> 43:55.549
So many tears are falling.

43:56.842 --> 43:58.510
[sniffles]
I know.

44:02.973 --> 44:04.391
The coffee is wonderful.

44:08.896 --> 44:10.898
[both sigh]

44:11.815 --> 44:14.985
[both laughing]

44:34.338 --> 44:36.340
[light music playing]

44:48.477 --> 44:50.604
[doctor] She's extremely dehydrated.

44:50.688 --> 44:54.274
Her hemoglobin levels are much lower
than I'd like to see.

44:54.358 --> 44:56.527
Her electrolytes are expectedly low, too.

44:57.861 --> 45:00.280
So we've given her
some fluids intravenously,

45:00.364 --> 45:01.698
and she's got a prescription.

45:01.782 --> 45:03.867
She needs to finish her IV,
and then she'll be good to go.

45:04.660 --> 45:06.995
So she doesn't need
to stay here overnight?

45:07.079 --> 45:08.580
You can take her home.

45:08.664 --> 45:11.208
Just make sure she's eating,
and she needs rest.

45:12.000 --> 45:14.378
Right now, she needs to keep
stress levels down.

45:14.461 --> 45:16.380
I hope you and your sister
can help with that.

45:16.964 --> 45:18.507
It's our responsibility to our parents.

45:19.508 --> 45:20.968
Okay. Thank you.

45:28.100 --> 45:30.936
[Ha-kyung] She's dehydrated.
But she can come home.

45:31.019 --> 45:34.148
We can take care of her.
She needs to relax.

45:34.231 --> 45:35.107
[Tae-kyung] You hear that?

45:37.985 --> 45:39.695
- It wasn't about me.
- You stressed her out.

45:39.778 --> 45:41.071
It's about my work.
[shushes]

45:41.780 --> 45:44.074
- I'm a director now. It's different.
- Be quiet.

45:44.158 --> 45:46.201
- [both chuckle]
- Look who's feeling better now.

45:48.370 --> 45:51.498
- [Mrs. Bae] I'm so glad you're here.
- [Tae-kyung] Mom's smiling.

46:02.009 --> 46:05.804
MOTEL

46:16.690 --> 46:17.983
Ten million won.

46:18.609 --> 46:21.069
This is all that I have.
This is the last time, okay?

46:21.653 --> 46:23.071
All that I have, I've given you.

46:26.158 --> 46:27.618
I knew it.

46:28.494 --> 46:31.955
Your girlfriend's better
at opening your wallet than I'll ever be.

46:32.998 --> 46:34.208
Right?

46:34.291 --> 46:37.377
Director Jin Ha-kyung. I know everything.

46:39.004 --> 46:41.215
She's obviously on the old side.

46:41.298 --> 46:43.091
She's awful pretty, though.

46:43.675 --> 46:46.386
She looks all delicate.
A real classy type.

46:46.470 --> 46:50.390
By the way, how far up
the ladder as a director at the KMA?

46:50.474 --> 46:52.267
I bet her paycheck's high.

46:52.351 --> 46:53.894
I get it.

46:53.977 --> 46:56.605
You're just like your old man.
Get a girl who'll take care of you.

46:56.688 --> 46:58.440
Right? I see you.

46:59.107 --> 47:02.903
Dad, you're saying you met
Director Jin in person?

47:06.615 --> 47:08.575
Well, didn't you come 'cause she said to?

47:11.370 --> 47:14.498
See, I really need money.

47:14.581 --> 47:16.250
And I needed it yesterday, right?

47:16.833 --> 47:18.877
Would you find it in your heart
to lend me any?

47:21.505 --> 47:25.050
'Cause my boy, Si-woo, he's great.
I love that kid.

47:25.634 --> 47:28.303
Well, except his cash.
[snickers]

47:28.929 --> 47:33.058
I guess if he gets switched to HQ,
he's not a total idiot.

47:33.141 --> 47:34.685
But he tells me he's still broke.

47:38.689 --> 47:43.318
I say that it's time for your investment
if you really like my boy.

47:44.069 --> 47:45.946
Ten million won should do it.

47:52.077 --> 47:53.829
You've actually lost it.

47:53.912 --> 47:55.539
What, it worked out.

47:56.498 --> 48:01.295
Hey. Hey, hey. In my eyes,
it just means she really does like you.

48:01.378 --> 48:04.631
She's loads better than that other chick.
Ugh, the reporter, the dumb one?

48:04.715 --> 48:06.425
I like this one better.

48:06.508 --> 48:09.970
And this one, she's so my style.

48:10.679 --> 48:13.557
Anyway, it means a lot, kid.
Here. Use this for a taxi.

48:13.640 --> 48:14.766
[grumbles]

48:14.850 --> 48:16.893
[breathes heavily]

48:16.977 --> 48:19.563
Disrespect.
You're gonna grab your old man?

48:19.646 --> 48:20.731
Let go!

48:20.814 --> 48:22.399
Why did you ruin everything?

48:22.482 --> 48:25.027
- What did I do?
- You ruined everything!

48:26.111 --> 48:27.821
You're ruining my life.

48:29.323 --> 48:30.407
Leave me alone.

48:31.992 --> 48:33.827
Please, please just stay away from me.

48:34.453 --> 48:35.829
Stay away.

48:46.715 --> 48:49.134
That asshole.

48:50.302 --> 48:52.304
[somber music playing]

49:01.146 --> 49:03.732
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

49:06.568 --> 49:07.611
[sighs]

49:11.823 --> 49:13.116
[Tae-kyung] Mom.

49:15.369 --> 49:16.495
[groans]

49:21.375 --> 49:23.085
Have some food before you go.

49:23.168 --> 49:24.503
Don't worry, Mom.

49:24.586 --> 49:26.588
There's bulgogi and radish kimchi.

49:27.297 --> 49:30.050
It's what Tae-kyung brought you
when she stopped by the other day.

49:30.133 --> 49:31.093
Have you had any?

49:34.388 --> 49:36.973
What? Did you get it
from the guy upstairs?

49:37.557 --> 49:38.600
What are you saying?

49:38.684 --> 49:41.520
I had to. You changed the door code
and don't answer your phone.

49:41.603 --> 49:43.480
You should have left it at the front desk.

49:44.231 --> 49:45.107
I…

49:45.190 --> 49:48.360
It would've gone bad.
You can't leave bulgogi out.

49:48.443 --> 49:50.821
Enough. Stop. It's all right.

49:51.405 --> 49:53.907
I need a glass of water.
[groans]

49:54.866 --> 49:58.286
Mm.
[stomping]

50:01.206 --> 50:02.624
Her neighbors are weird.

50:02.708 --> 50:05.001
Why wouldn't he call and give it to her?

50:06.545 --> 50:07.713
Seemed like he lived alone.

50:07.796 --> 50:09.506
[Tae-kyung gasps]
No.

50:09.589 --> 50:11.299
The pig ate it on his own?

50:13.343 --> 50:15.345
[playful music playing]

50:16.012 --> 50:18.807
DOES IT SMELL?
NATURAL MINERAL PRESERVATIVE

50:18.890 --> 50:20.892
- [slams]
- [sighs]

50:30.026 --> 50:32.028
[beeping]

50:32.112 --> 50:34.740
- [device ringing]
- [sighs]

50:35.323 --> 50:37.576
CALLING
APARTMENT 1201

50:38.535 --> 50:42.456
How in the hell is this woman
still not home? It's been days!

50:42.956 --> 50:43.790
[sighs]

50:43.874 --> 50:46.001
You're not gonna realize
your food is missing?

50:47.127 --> 50:47.961
[groans]

50:48.044 --> 50:50.922
How long do I have to keep it?
I'll toss it someday!

50:51.882 --> 50:54.050
It all stinks!
[grunts]

50:57.637 --> 50:58.513
[sighs]

50:59.389 --> 51:00.599
[grumbles]

51:08.148 --> 51:09.941
Tae-kyung, get Mom's water.

51:16.656 --> 51:17.491
[sighs]

51:21.703 --> 51:22.913
[clanks]

51:26.082 --> 51:28.627
- [plastic rustles]
- [objects clank]

51:33.840 --> 51:36.176
[box clicking]

51:48.605 --> 51:49.648
Is Han Ki-jun here?

51:50.732 --> 51:53.068
I don't know.
I haven't seen him yet today.

51:54.945 --> 51:57.239
[sighs]
I hope he finished.

51:58.865 --> 52:00.158
[exhales heavily]

52:03.829 --> 52:04.996
What do I do?

52:05.997 --> 52:07.082
What do I do?

52:08.375 --> 52:09.626
I'll get fired.

52:10.794 --> 52:11.962
I don't know.

52:12.504 --> 52:13.797
[sighs]

52:16.383 --> 52:18.760
[Ki-jun] Ha-kyung, it's me.

52:18.844 --> 52:22.055
I'm sorry, but can you help me
with the column last time?

52:22.848 --> 52:26.810
[grumbling]
Damn it! Are you crazy?

52:26.893 --> 52:29.688
Come on. Come on. Come on.
I can't text her. I can't.

52:29.771 --> 52:32.357
No, I shouldn't. Oh, what do I do?

52:32.440 --> 52:33.900
What do I do?

52:33.984 --> 52:35.610
I have to… I have to call her.

52:36.361 --> 52:37.445
Damn it.

52:40.574 --> 52:42.033
[line rings]

52:42.742 --> 52:43.994
Oh, Ha-kyung, hey.

52:44.077 --> 52:45.370
[nervous chuckle]

52:45.453 --> 52:47.664
How's night shift treating you?
You must be tired.

52:48.999 --> 52:50.917
Uh, I called, because…

52:55.839 --> 52:57.424
You have to save me.

52:58.884 --> 53:00.260
I'm sorry, I am.

53:01.052 --> 53:05.807
One last time, save me.
Can you do the column, huh?

53:35.545 --> 53:37.923
So, how's your mom doing?

53:39.132 --> 53:40.675
She's well. Thank you.

53:41.676 --> 53:42.802
That's good news.

53:42.886 --> 53:43.803
[chuckles]

53:50.852 --> 53:52.062
I'm so sorry.

53:52.145 --> 53:52.979
For what?

53:56.149 --> 53:57.150
For my dad.

54:01.196 --> 54:02.447
I had no idea.

54:07.285 --> 54:09.371
I can't even say how sorry I am.

54:10.497 --> 54:11.581
Are you hungry?

54:19.881 --> 54:20.840
Go ahead.

54:21.883 --> 54:23.969
My mom always makes it from scratch.

54:25.261 --> 54:28.139
It's a tradition for us.
We make it in the summer every year.

54:29.516 --> 54:30.350
Why?

54:31.810 --> 54:33.853
It's almost the anniversary
of my dad's death,

54:34.854 --> 54:36.481
and this was his favorite thing to eat.

54:49.911 --> 54:51.329
Mmm…

54:52.998 --> 54:55.375
This is actually good.
I guess Ha-kyung's a chef like you.

54:55.458 --> 54:57.919
If you forget she complained
the whole time, it's great.

54:59.087 --> 55:00.380
Is she gonna visit?

55:01.840 --> 55:02.674
What do you think?

55:03.508 --> 55:04.926
Don't hold your breath.

55:05.010 --> 55:06.803
You know how she is about work.

55:10.598 --> 55:11.808
[sighs]

55:12.684 --> 55:13.977
You're right, she did well.

55:17.564 --> 55:21.359
[Ha-kyung] The day my father died
is probably the day

55:22.110 --> 55:24.154
I'd most like to erase from my memory.

55:24.821 --> 55:27.198
[door closes]

55:28.533 --> 55:30.118
I'm back. Hello?

55:38.126 --> 55:39.252
Mama?

55:51.765 --> 55:53.266
Is anybody home?

55:58.813 --> 56:01.024
[whimpers]

56:08.406 --> 56:10.408
[ominous music playing]

56:27.550 --> 56:29.761
[Ha-kyung] His business went under
and it hit him hard.

56:31.012 --> 56:33.890
He took it so hard
that he thought he had to disappear.

56:36.518 --> 56:39.145
[sobbing]

56:43.358 --> 56:45.693
So that's where I'm at with my dad.

56:47.278 --> 56:51.950
So you don't have to worry
that I'll judge you at all with your dad.

56:53.827 --> 56:58.164
[Si-woo] "When one cloud meets another,
there's a great noise, thunder.

56:58.248 --> 57:00.750
Like them, I want to meet you,

57:01.417 --> 57:04.921
shouting about it from the rooftops
without a thought."

57:10.844 --> 57:12.846
[light music playing]

57:23.356 --> 57:24.774
It's really good.

57:24.858 --> 57:25.984
[chuckles]

57:28.069 --> 57:30.655
[Si-woo] "When one cloud
suddenly meets another cloud,

57:30.738 --> 57:33.324
There's a great light, too, lightning.

57:33.408 --> 57:35.076
With that light when I meet you,

57:35.910 --> 57:38.788
I'll see the path
I strayed from long ago."

57:40.123 --> 57:41.541
Can you promise me one thing?

57:47.547 --> 57:48.381
What is it?

57:49.924 --> 57:51.885
If things change
and you don't want to be with me,

57:52.760 --> 57:54.262
I want to be the first to know.

57:55.388 --> 57:58.433
Even if you're having doubts,
don't be afraid to let me know.

58:02.061 --> 58:04.689
I know I'd be heartbroken
if your feelings changed

58:04.772 --> 58:05.607
and we called it off.

58:05.690 --> 58:07.233
But it hurts even more…

58:09.194 --> 58:11.237
if I don't see it coming at all.

58:14.532 --> 58:15.617
That happened with him.

58:24.667 --> 58:26.252
And with Ki-jun, too.

58:32.091 --> 58:34.677
Tell me that I won't be surprised by you.

58:37.388 --> 58:40.058
[Si-woo] "You shine brightly
when you tell me…

58:40.934 --> 58:45.355
that rain needs to meet another rain
for them to get drenched."

58:47.357 --> 58:48.358
I promise you.

58:50.777 --> 58:51.945
Okay, good.

58:58.493 --> 58:59.911
Well, then let's live together.

59:04.958 --> 59:06.000
THEMED STORY FOR JULY

59:06.084 --> 59:07.544
[Ki-jun] Ready to print.

59:08.211 --> 59:09.254
[Ju-won] Let's see.

59:10.046 --> 59:12.674
Assistant Director Kim did decent work.

59:12.757 --> 59:15.635
And I hope you consider his column,
just consider mine, too.

59:15.718 --> 59:17.178
I'll respect whichever you pick.

59:17.262 --> 59:18.721
Okay, very good.

59:18.805 --> 59:19.806
Okay.

59:20.848 --> 59:22.809
[chuckles]

59:25.103 --> 59:26.271
Good work.

59:26.854 --> 59:29.065
I should really be saying that to you.

59:30.316 --> 59:32.860
I did wanna warn you the director
has a habit of thinking

59:32.944 --> 59:34.988
things need to change
when he just needs to relax.

59:35.071 --> 59:36.155
Huh?

59:36.698 --> 59:38.741
Oh, yeah.
Well, at least I got the experience.

59:38.825 --> 59:41.661
That's right, you did.
And you're gonna go far.

59:41.744 --> 59:43.496
You did well, for sure.

59:43.580 --> 59:47.083
Ah, the mighty Han Ki-jun is back.

59:47.166 --> 59:48.793
I want this sent
to the printer right away.

59:48.876 --> 59:51.629
Yes, I'll do it now.
I'll send the column myself.

59:53.006 --> 59:56.217
I knew it was still in there.
[chuckling]

01:00:01.222 --> 01:00:02.515
[cell phone buzzes]

01:00:08.938 --> 01:00:11.107
WILL YOU BE LATE?
I THINK SO. YOU CAN GO TO BED FIRST.

01:00:11.190 --> 01:00:13.026
[Yu-jin] Can we meet up for a sec?

01:00:14.652 --> 01:00:15.737
Hm…

01:00:20.867 --> 01:00:22.994
What's going on? I'm sure you're busy.

01:00:23.786 --> 01:00:25.121
You want a drink? It's on me.

01:00:26.748 --> 01:00:29.417
Anyway, were you able to register us?

01:00:29.500 --> 01:00:31.628
If we're all set,
then we can look into the loan.

01:00:31.711 --> 01:00:33.463
We don't have much longer
in the apartment.

01:00:34.172 --> 01:00:37.175
Well, that's kinda
what I wanted to talk about.

01:00:37.842 --> 01:00:38.926
Ah, what's up?

01:00:40.762 --> 01:00:45.391
I wanna hold off
on officially registering anything.

01:00:47.852 --> 01:00:48.853
Huh?

01:00:52.857 --> 01:00:56.027
You think I should live with you?

01:00:56.611 --> 01:00:59.489
Mm-hm. It'll make me so happy.

01:01:01.199 --> 01:01:03.451
You could live here. Say you will.

01:01:03.534 --> 01:01:05.495
["Promise You" by Kyuhyun playing]

01:01:08.331 --> 01:01:10.041
What do you mean, hold off?

01:01:10.833 --> 01:01:11.793
Wait.

01:01:12.502 --> 01:01:14.087
What are you saying right now?

01:01:14.170 --> 01:01:15.963
Why would you want to put it off?

01:01:17.006 --> 01:01:19.509
Why? Because of me?

01:01:22.136 --> 01:01:23.930
I just think it would be smart.

01:01:29.686 --> 01:01:32.146
["Promise You" by Kyuhyun playing]

01:02:05.263 --> 01:02:09.350
Today, we can expect to have
over 0.3ppm ozone concentration.

01:02:09.434 --> 01:02:12.437
[driver] The weather is perfectly fine.
What's with the ozone warning?

01:02:12.520 --> 01:02:14.981
Who is handling the complaint calls
that came into Team Two today?

01:02:15.064 --> 01:02:16.691
I didn't do all that work in school

01:02:16.774 --> 01:02:19.235
only to come here at work
in a call center.

01:02:19.944 --> 01:02:22.613
We are here to do that kind of work.

01:02:23.656 --> 01:02:24.699
Go ahead if you want.

01:02:24.782 --> 01:02:26.159
- Huh?
- Divorce.

01:02:26.242 --> 01:02:28.870
[director 2] Haven't you heard
they're living in the night-duty room?

01:02:29.412 --> 01:02:31.289
[Ha-kyung] Did you just say both of them?

01:02:32.373 --> 01:02:33.624
[Ha-kyung gasps]
Lee Si-woo…

01:02:34.500 --> 01:02:37.170
[reporter 2] Her husband works
at the KMA, you know?

01:02:38.546 --> 01:02:42.550
[Si-woo] I think Ki-jun found out
that you and I lived together.
